NAME
    if - conditional command execution

SYNOPSIS
    if LIST; then LIST; [elif LIST; then LIST;] ... [else LIST;] fi

DESCRIPTION
    Executes the condition LIST after 'if'. If its final exit status is
    0, executes the 'then' body and finishes. Otherwise evaluates each
    'elif' condition in order, running the body of the first that exits
    0, or the 'else' body if present and no condition succeeded.

    Multi-line blocks work both interactively (with a '> ' continuation
    prompt until 'fi') and inside scripts run via source(1).

EXAMPLES
    if [ -f /Logs/run.log ]; then echo found; else echo missing; fi
    if command -v grep; then echo ok; fi

EXIT STATUS
    0   No branch ran, or the executed branch exited 0.
    N   Exit status of the last command in the executed branch.

SEE ALSO
    test(1), [(1), for(1), while(1)
